<exercisegroup xml:id="exercisegroup-diagonalization-poly-from-form">

<title>Extracting information from diagonal form</title>

<introduction><p>
	In each case,
	assume that <m> A </m> is similar to the given diagonal matrix.
	State the eigenvalues of <m> A </m>,
	the algebraic multiplicity of each eigenvalue,
	and the characteristic polynomial of <m> A </m>.
</p></introduction>

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m>\displaystyle \begin{bmatrix} -1 \\ \amp 4 \end{bmatrix} </m></p></statement>

	<answer>
		<p> <m> \lambda = -1, 4 </m>, each with multiplicity <m> 1 </m>. </p>
		<p><m> c_A(\lambda) = (\lambda + 1) (\lambda - 4) </m></p>
	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m>\displaystyle \begin{bmatrix} -2 \\ \amp 0 \\ \amp \amp 0 \end{bmatrix} </m></p></statement>

	<answer>
		<p>
			<m> \lambda_1 = -2 </m> with multiplicity <m> 1 </m>;
			<m> \lambda_2 =  0 </m> with multiplicity <m> 2 </m>.
		</p>
		<p><m> c_A(\lambda) = {\lambda}^2 (\lambda + 2) </m></p>
	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m>\displaystyle \begin{bmatrix} -8 \\ \amp -2 \\ \amp \amp 5 \\ \amp \amp \amp -8 \end{bmatrix} </m></p></statement>

	<answer>
		<p>
			<m> \lambda_1 = -8 </m> with multiplicity <m> 2 </m>;
			<m> \lambda_2 = -2 </m> with multiplicity <m> 1 </m>;
			<m> \lambda_3 =  5 </m> with multiplicity <m> 1 </m>.
		</p>
		<p><m> c_A(\lambda) = {(\lambda + 8)}^2 (\lambda + 2) (\lambda - 5) </m></p>
	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m>\displaystyle
		\begin{bmatrix}
			6 \\
			\amp 6 \\
			\amp \amp 6 \\
			\amp \amp \amp 7 \\
			\amp \amp \amp \amp 7 \\
			\amp \amp \amp \amp \amp 1 \\
			\amp \amp \amp \amp \amp \amp -3 \\
		\end{bmatrix}
	</m></p></statement>

	<answer>
		<p>
			<m> \lambda_1 =  6 </m> with multiplicity <m> 3 </m>;
			<m> \lambda_2 =  7 </m> with multiplicity <m> 2 </m>;
			<m> \lambda_3 =  1 </m> with multiplicity <m> 1 </m>;
			<m> \lambda_4 = -3 </m> with multiplicity <m> 1 </m>.
		</p>
		<p><m> c_A(\lambda) = {(\lambda - 6)}^3 {(\lambda - 7)}^2 (\lambda - 1) (\lambda + 3) </m></p>
	</answer>

</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
